# API Routes

## Handler Shape

```typescript
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  try {
    const session = await auth()
    if (!session?.user || session.user.role !== "admin") {
      return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 })
    }
    // ... logic
    return NextResponse.json(data, { status: 200 })
  } catch (error: any) {
    console.error("Error fetching X:", error)
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: error.message || "Failed to fetch X" },
      { status: 500 }
    )
  }
}
```

## Auth by Namespace

- `admin/` — require `session.user.role === "admin"`
- `coach/` — require coach role
- `public/` — no auth; read-only catalog/franchise data
- `user/`, `enrollments/` — authenticated parent or student
- `cron/` — verify Vercel cron secret or internal auth
- `payments/webhook` — Stripe signature, not session auth

## Data Access

- V2 catalog CRUD: query `v2_*` tables via `supabaseAdmin` — follow `database-schema` rule
- Reference implementations: `src/app/api/admin/*/v2/` routes
- Auth/enrollment/payment: `@/lib/db`, `@/lib/permissions`
- Validate dynamic fields against `offering_schema` / `instance_schema` before insert/update

## Special Cases

Stripe webhooks need `export const runtime = 'nodejs'`, `dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`, and raw body via `req.text()`.
